{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Digipin\/documentation\/Digipin"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/digipin"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"text":"A Swift implementation of India’s Digital Postal Index Number (DIGIPIN).","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Digipin is a lightweight, offline-first Swift library for generating and decoding ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"DIGIPIN"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" codes from geographic coordinates.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"DIGIPIN is a national geo-coded addressing system defined by the Department of Posts, Government of India. It divides the country into uniform grid cells of approximately "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"4m × 4m","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", assigning each cell a deterministic 10-character alphanumeric code derived purely from latitude and longitude."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"digipin-social-preview"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This package focuses on deterministic and repeatable results, operates entirely offline without any network or external dependencies, preserves user privacy by relying solely on coordinate-based computation, and fully complies with the official DIGIPIN specification published in March 2025."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Use Cases","type":"heading","anchor":"Use-Cases"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Digipin is suitable for logistics and last-mile delivery systems, address normalization and deduplication workflows, emergency response platforms, fintech KYC and verification flows, and any application that requires precise, offline location identification within India."}],